      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "1f08b8da47aee2c134d642d01edfb0e0",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"tensor-intuition-in-pytorch\">Tensor Intuition in PyTorch</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This notebook keeps the code visible on purpose.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The goal is not to memorize PyTorch syntax. The goal is to build one clear picture:</span>\n<ul>\n<li>a <strong>tensor</strong> is a container of numbers with a shape</li>\n<li>shapes tell us how data is organized</li>\n<li>PyTorch gives us direct operations for indexing, dot products, and matrix multiplication</li>\n<li>for these examples, we stay on the <strong>CPU</strong> so the ideas stay simple</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Read the code, run your eye over the shapes, and connect each operation to the kind of object it acts on.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "vblA",
      "code_hash": "067876ffcf8d07a4cf31835507626916",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"the-architecture-of-data\">The Architecture of Data</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A tensor is simply a container of numbers with a specific <strong>shape</strong>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Instead of thinking of tensors as advanced mathematical objects, think of them as the physical layout of your data. The shape tells us exactly how the numbers are arranged.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "bkHC",
      "code_hash": "d7c2d5b8da0cf412ee80f16860ec1185",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": ""
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "lEQa",
      "code_hash": "7ecbe141091048aba333efbd8c264009",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<div style='display: flex;flex: 1;flex-direction: column;justify-content: flex-start;align-items: normal;flex-wrap: nowrap;gap: 0.5rem'><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">When you see a shape like <code>(4, 2)</code>, it is telling you a story:</span>\n<ul>\n<li>We are processing <code>4</code> examples simultaneously.</li>\n<li>Each example has <code>2</code> distinct features.</li>\n</ul></span><marimo-ui-element object-id='lEQa-0' random-id='6e16570d-5adf-b396-b0a4-6b1d7407e4f7'><marimo-table data-initial-value='[]' data-label='null' data-data='&quot;[{&#92;&quot;name&#92;&quot;:&#92;&quot;scalar&#92;&quot;,&#92;&quot;shape&#92;&quot;:&#92;&quot;()&#92;&quot;,&#92;&quot;example&#92;&quot;:&#92;&quot;tensor(3.)&#92;&quot;},{&#92;&quot;name&#92;&quot;:&#92;&quot;vector&#92;&quot;,&#92;&quot;shape&#92;&quot;:&#92;&quot;(3,)&#92;&quot;,&#92;&quot;example&#92;&quot;:&#92;&quot;tensor([   3.,    2., 1500.])&#92;&quot;},{&#92;&quot;name&#92;&quot;:&#92;&quot;batch&#92;&quot;,&#92;&quot;shape&#92;&quot;:&#92;&quot;(4, 2)&#92;&quot;,&#92;&quot;example&#92;&quot;:&#92;&quot;tensor([[3., 2.],&#92;&#92;n        [4., 3.],&#92;&#92;n        [2., 1.],&#92;&#92;n        [5., 4.]])&#92;&quot;}]&quot;' data-total-rows='3' data-total-columns='3' data-max-columns='50' data-banner-text='&quot;&quot;' data-pagination='false' data-page-size='10' data-selection='&quot;multi&quot;' data-show-filters='false' data-show-download='false' data-show-column-summaries='false' data-show-data-types='true' data-show-page-size-selector='false' data-show-column-explorer='true' data-show-chart-builder='true' data-row-headers='[]' data-has-stable-row-id='false' data-lazy='false' data-preload='false' data-download-file-name='&quot;rows&quot;'></marimo-table></marimo-ui-element></div>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "PKri",
      "code_hash": "bd6635010c780b5d211fe3c62938d446",
